  "description": "The founding case of the suite. After a KERI 2.0 inception, an attachments group (-C) holds a controller signature group (-K) of three Ed25519 indexed signatures and then a witness signature group (-L) of one. -K has size 66 (3 x 22 quadlets), not 3; -L has size 22, not 1; -C has size 90. A second inception and its attachments follow. A parser that counts items reads 66 as 66 signatures, runs past -K and loses the stream. The symbol legends of the Encoding Scheme Symbols Table (line 674) and the indexed-code symbol table (line 714), and the Examples text at line 1103, say a count code's digits count 'Primitives or groups'; this case rests on the explicit rule at line 591 instead.",
